# Haemophilia A (factor VIII deficiency) — X-linked recessive.
# Every daughter of an affected man inherits his X, so II-2 and II-3 are obligate
# carriers by deduction; III-3 was confirmed by factor VIII assay.
# III-2 and III-3 are first cousins: their mothers are sisters.
pedigree "Haemophilia A — Four-Generation Family"
  I-1 [male, affected, deceased]
  I-2 [female, unaffected]
  I-1 -- I-2
    II-2 [female, obligate-carrier]
    II-3 [female, obligate-carrier]

  II-1 [male, unaffected]
  II-4 [male, unaffected]

  II-1 -- II-2
    III-1 [male, affected]
    III-2 [male, unaffected]

  II-3 -- II-4
    III-3 [female, carrier-x]
    III-4 [male, unaffected]

  III-2 == III-3
    IV-1 [male, affected, proband]
    IV-2 [unknown, sab]
    IV-3 [female, carrier-x, twin-mz]
    IV-4 [female, carrier-x, twin-mz]
